---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { TRACKS, topicsInTrack } from '../data/topics';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base title="All topics | spring-framework-learnings" current="tracks">
  <main class="shell">
    <article>
      <h1>All topics</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Everything, grouped by track, including what is not written yet. If you are here to learn
        rather than to look something up, <a href={`${base}/`}>start here</a> instead — this page is
        a map, not a path.
      </p>

      <div class="tracks">
        {
          TRACKS.map((track) => (
            <section class="track">
              <h2>{track.title}</h2>
              <p class="blurb">{track.blurb}</p>
              {topicsInTrack(track.id).map((topic) => (
                <div class={`topic ${topic.status}`}>
                  <span class={`dot ${topic.status}`} />
                  <span class="name">
                    {topic.status === 'shipped' ? (
                      <a href={`${base}/notes/${topic.slug}`}>{topic.title}</a>
                    ) : (
                      topic.title
                    )}
                  </span>
                  {topic.tests && <span class="tests">{topic.tests} tests</span>}
                </div>
              ))}
            </section>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <h2 id="method">How these notes are written</h2>
      <p>
        The order matters, because writing the prose first produces notes that sound right and are
        not. Read the implementation. Write a test that would fail if the claim were wrong in either
        direction. Only then write the explanation, with a pointer to the test underneath it.
      </p>
      <p>
        That discipline has caught this project being wrong repeatedly:
        <code>AnnotationUtils.getAnnotation</code> stops one meta-level out and returns null rather
        than failing; the native <code>@Retryable</code>'s <code>maxRetries</code> counts differently
        from <code>spring-retry</code>'s <code>maxAttempts</code>; injection fires before an
        unordered <code>BeanPostProcessor</code> sees the properties callback. Each of those was a
        confident paragraph until a test disagreed.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
